Z||000000||Philphine||10-02-2000||12:53 PM||||<BR>the pair actually. just got the scoops rockcrawl auctioned off on ebay. they look good and fit the contour of the location good. i don't know when i'll get them on but i'm happy with them. i sure didn't want to ask while the auction was going on but i wondered why more people didn't bid. i figured they're smaller than other available scoops and not as showy but unless you can make something yourself they are about 1/2 the price of the next available scoop (i guess that would depend on whatever price he sets or how the next auction goes). i need to leave pos feedback on ebay when i have more time but bettween us forum folks i'm saying this is a good deal. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill) that now has a pair of cheap (but nice) scoops.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 10-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||10-02-2000||07:06 PM||||Phil, thanks for the great compliments. <P> I have another pair on Ebay right now, as well as a single one. After that I have two more pairs that need to be completed. I really don't have the time right now to continue making them, so that will be it for a long time. I've had a few offers from people to either buy the molds, or to act as dealers for me. I'm undecided as to what I will do. I definately cannot fulfill the demand for these! Anybody here with fiberglass experience and some extra time?! <P>Here are the links to the Ebay auctions: <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=449945164&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=449945164&r=0&t=0</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=449964888&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=449964888&r=0&t=0</A> <P>Well I just realized they are ending in two hours!<P>Thanks again Phil for the compliments.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
